.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt OCSP_RESPONSE_STATUS 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm OCSP_response_status ,
.Nm OCSP_response_get1_basic ,
.Nm OCSP_response_create ,
.Nm OCSP_RESPONSE_free ,
.Nm OCSP_RESPID_set_by_name ,
.Nm OCSP_RESPID_set_by_key_ex ,
.Nm OCSP_RESPID_set_by_key ,
.Nm OCSP_RESPID_match_ex ,
.Nm OCSP_RESPID_match ,
.Nm OCSP_basic_sign ,
.Nm OCSP_basic_sign_ctx
.Nd OCSP response functions
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/ocsp.h
.Ft int
.Fo OCSP_response_status
.Fa "OCSP_RESPONSE *resp"
.Fc
.Ft OCSP_BASICRESP *
.Fo OCSP_response_get1_basic
.Fa "OCSP_RESPONSE *resp"
.Fc
.Ft OCSP_RESPONSE *
.Fo OCSP_response_create
.Fa "int status"
.Fa "OCSP_BASICRESP *bs"
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo OCSP_RESPONSE_free
.Fa "OCSP_RESPONSE *resp"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo OCSP_RESPID_set_by_name
.Fa "OCSP_RESPID *respid"
.Fa "X509 *cert"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo OCSP_RESPID_set_by_key_ex
.Fa "OCSP_RESPID *respid"
.Fa "X509 *cert"
.Fa "OSSL_LIB_CTX *libctx"
.Fa "const char *propq"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo OCSP_RESPID_set_by_key
.Fa "OCSP_RESPID *respid"
.Fa "X509 *cert"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo OCSP_RESPID_match_ex
.Fa "OCSP_RESPID *respid"
.Fa "X509 *cert"
.Fa "OSSL_LIB_CTX *libctx"
.Fa "const char *propq"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo OCSP_RESPID_match
.Fa "OCSP_RESPID *respid"
.Fa "X509 *cert"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo OCSP_basic_sign
.Fa "OCSP_BASICRESP *brsp"
.Fa "X509 *signer"
.Fa "EVP_PKEY *key"
.Fa "const EVP_MD *dgst"
.Fa "STACK_OF(X509) *certs"
.Fa "unsigned long flags"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo OCSP_basic_sign_ctx
.Fa "OCSP_BASICRESP *brsp"
.Fa "X509 *signer"
.Fa "EVP_MD_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "STACK_OF(X509) *certs"
.Fa "unsigned long flags"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn OCSP_response_status
returns the OCSP response status of
.Fa resp .
It returns one of the values:
.Em OCSP_RESPONSE_STATUS_SUCCESSFUL ,
.Em OCSP_RESPONSE_STATUS_MALFORMEDREQUEST ,
.Em OCSP_RESPONSE_STATUS_INTERNALERROR ,
.Em OCSP_RESPONSE_STATUS_TRYLATER
.Em OCSP_RESPONSE_STATUS_SIGREQUIRED ,
or
.Em OCSP_RESPONSE_STATUS_UNAUTHORIZED .
.Pp
.Fn OCSP_response_get1_basic
decodes and returns the
.Vt OCSP_BASICRESP
structure contained in
.Fa resp .
.Pp
.Fn OCSP_response_create
creates and returns an
.Vt OCSP_RESPONSE
structure for
.Fa status
and optionally including basic response
.Fa bs .
.Pp
.Fn OCSP_RESPONSE_free
frees up OCSP response
.Fa resp .
If the argument is NULL, nothing is done.
.Pp
.Fn OCSP_RESPID_set_by_name
sets the name of the OCSP_RESPID to be the same as the subject name in
the supplied X509 certificate
.Fa cert
for the OCSP responder.
.Pp
.Fn OCSP_RESPID_set_by_key_ex
sets the key of the OCSP_RESPID to be the same as the key in the
supplied X509 certificate
.Fa cert
for the OCSP responder.
The key is stored as a SHA1 hash.
To calculate the hash the SHA1 algorithm is fetched using the library
ctx
.Fa libctx
and the property query string
.Fa propq
(see
.Xr crypto 7
for further information).
.Pp
.Fn OCSP_RESPID_set_by_key
does the same as
.Fn OCSP_RESPID_set_by_key_ex
except that the default library context is used with an empty property
query string.
.Pp
Note that an OCSP_RESPID can only have one of the name, or the key set.
Calling
.Fn OCSP_RESPID_set_by_name
or
.Fn OCSP_RESPID_set_by_key
will clear any existing setting.
.Pp
.Fn OCSP_RESPID_match_ex
tests whether the OCSP_RESPID given in
.Fa respid
matches with the X509 certificate
.Fa cert
based on the SHA1 hash.
To calculate the hash the SHA1 algorithm is fetched using the library
ctx
.Fa libctx
and the property query string
.Fa propq
(see
.Xr crypto 7
for further information).
.Pp
.Fn OCSP_RESPID_match
does the same as
.Fn OCSP_RESPID_match_ex
except that the default library context is used with an empty property
query string.
.Pp
.Fn OCSP_basic_sign
signs OCSP response
.Fa brsp
using certificate
.Fa signer ,
private key
.Fa key ,
digest
.Fa dgst
and additional certificates
.Fa certs .
If the
.Fa flags
option
.Em OCSP_NOCERTS
is set then no certificates will be included in the response.
If the
.Fa flags
option
.Em OCSP_RESPID_KEY
is set then the responder is identified by key ID rather than by name.
.Fn OCSP_basic_sign_ctx
also signs OCSP response
.Fa brsp
but uses the parameters contained in digest context
.Fa ctx .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Xr OCSP_RESPONSE_status 3
returns a status value.
.Pp
.Fn OCSP_response_get1_basic
returns an
.Vt OCSP_BASICRESP
structure pointer or
.Dv NULL
if an error occurred.
.Pp
.Fn OCSP_response_create
returns an
.Vt OCSP_RESPONSE
structure pointer or
.Dv NULL
if an error occurred.
.Pp
.Fn OCSP_RESPONSE_free
does not return a value.
.Pp
.Fn OCSP_RESPID_set_by_name ,
.Fn OCSP_RESPID_set_by_key ,
.Fn OCSP_basic_sign ,
and
.Fn OCSP_basic_sign_ctx
return 1 on success or 0 on failure.
.Pp
.Fn OCSP_RESPID_match
returns 1 if the OCSP_RESPID and the X509 certificate match or 0
otherwise.
.Sh NOTES
.Fn OCSP_response_get1_basic
is only called if the status of a response is
.Em OCSP_RESPONSE_STATUS_SUCCESSFUL .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr crypto 7
.Xr OCSP_cert_to_id 3
.Xr OCSP_request_add1_nonce 3
.Xr OCSP_REQUEST_new 3
.Xr OCSP_resp_find_status 3
.Xr OCSP_sendreq_new 3
.Xr OCSP_RESPID_new 3
.Xr OCSP_RESPID_free 3
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn OCSP_RESPID_set_by_name ,
.Fn OCSP_RESPID_set_by_key
and
.Fn OCSP_RESPID_match
functions were added in OpenSSL 1.1.0a.
.Pp
The
.Fn OCSP_basic_sign_ctx
function was added in OpenSSL 1.1.1.
